  {
   "id": "greedy",
   "title": "The smallest load wins",
   "scene": {
    "parts": "plate",
    "strategy": "field_split",
    "spacing": 16,
    "field": 40
   },
   "notes": [
    "In an overlap the piece goes to the candidate whose load would be smallest <i>after</i> taking it: its load so far, the jump from where that laser stopped, the marking, and an optional proximity cost. With the metric <i>Exposure time</i> all of these are milliseconds from the <a href=\"laser_timing.html\">laser timing</a>.",
    "The comparison is <code>&lt;</code>, not <code>&lt;=</code>: on a tie the lower laser number wins, so every run gives the same result. The drawing uses a larger overlap so the sharing is easy to see."
   ],
   "ranges": [
    {
     "file": "lib/multi_laser/laser_assignment_math.js",
     "start": 434,
     "end": 456,
     "lines": [
      "function choose_laser_for_segment(a_candidates, a_states, a_a, a_b, a_fields, a_cost)",
      "{",
      "  let l_mid = lerp_point(a_a, a_b, 0.5);",
      "  if (a_candidates.length === 0) return find_nearest_laser(l_mid, a_fields);",
      "  if (a_candidates.length === 1) return a_candidates[0];",
      "",
      "  let r_index = a_candidates[0];",
      "  let l_best = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;",
      "  for (let i = 0; i < a_candidates.length; ++i)",
      "  {",
      "    let l_id = a_candidates[i];",
      "    let l_state = a_states[l_id];",
      "    let l_total = l_state.load + jump_cost(l_state.last_end, a_a, a_cost) + mark_cost(a_a, a_b, a_cost) +",
      "      proximity_cost(l_mid, l_id, a_fields, a_cost);",
      "    // '<' (not '<='): on a tie the lower laser index (earlier candidate) wins.",
      "    if (l_total < l_best)",
      "    {",
      "      l_best = l_total;",
      "      r_index = l_id;",
      "    }",
      "  }",
      "  return r_index;",
      "}"
     ],
     "marks": [
      12,
      15
     ]
    }
   ]
