  {
   "id": "lanes",
   "title": "Swimlanes, downstream first",
   "scene": {
    "parts": "parts",
    "strategy": "swimlane",
    "spacing": 20,
    "field": 80,
    "lane": 20
   },
   "notes": [
    "<code>build_swimlanes</code> cuts the platform into bands along the gas flow; lane 0 is the one furthest downstream. <code>assign_pieces_by_lane</code> then works lane by lane with fresh loads, so the lasers share every lane on its own.",
    "A swimlane piece is never split between lasers: the candidates are the fields that contain its centre. On one plate the hatch of a lane is a single piece, so balancing needs several parts or islands per lane, like the thirteen parts of the video in the drawing."
   ],
   "ranges": [
    {
     "file": "lib/multi_laser/scanner_array.js",
     "start": 196,
     "end": 204,
     "lines": [
      "  let l_count = Math.max(1, Math.ceil((l_max - l_min) / a_width));",
      "  let r_lanes = [];",
      "  for (let i = 0; i < l_count; ++i)",
      "  {",
      "    let l_lo = l_min + i * a_width;",
      "    let l_hi = (i === l_count - 1) ? l_max : (l_lo + a_width);",
      "    r_lanes.push({ lane_index: i, key_min: l_lo, key_max: l_hi });",
      "  }",
      "  return r_lanes;"
     ],
     "marks": [
